/** @mainpage Qore Markdown module

    Copyright 2026 Qore Technologies, s.r.o.

    @tableofcontents
    @section markdownintro Introduction

    The Markdown module converts Markdown text to HTML using the bundled Sundown
    1.16.0 parser. It supports tables, fenced code blocks, automatic links,
    strikethrough, and superscripts. Rendered HTML preserves raw HTML in the input;
    applications accepting untrusted documents must apply their own HTML policy.

    @section markdownexample Example
    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires markdown
string html = markdown_convert("# Invoice summary\n\n**Paid** in full.\n");
printf("%s", html);
    @endcode

    @section markdownfunctions Functions
    See @ref markdown_functions for the conversion and parser-version functions.

